WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.747
- I went to the DMV with
Willy Nelson one time.

00:00:03.747 --> 00:00:06.641
We both had to take our
driving test together

00:00:06.641 --> 00:00:09.322
or like the written part.

00:00:09.322 --> 00:00:14.001
So maybe studying with Willy
helped me to pass this.

00:00:14.001 --> 00:00:15.501
[Fast Paced Music]

00:00:23.548 --> 00:00:25.612
- When driving in fog,
you should use your:

00:00:25.612 --> 00:00:26.665
- A. High beams

00:00:26.665 --> 00:00:27.760
B. Low beams.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:29.126
C. Fog lights only.

00:00:29.126 --> 00:00:31.325
- Fog lights only says fog in it,

00:00:31.325 --> 00:00:32.281
but what if you're driving at night?

00:00:32.281 --> 00:00:33.953
You don't want to drive with fog lights on

00:00:33.953 --> 00:00:34.786
or your high beams.

00:00:34.786 --> 00:00:35.992
You want to go low beams.

00:00:35.992 --> 00:00:38.550
- Low beams, boom, drop the pencil.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:40.394
- I'm gonna go with low beams.

00:00:40.394 --> 00:00:43.304
High beams are reflective in the fog.

00:00:43.304 --> 00:00:45.009
- [Man] You are right.

00:00:45.009 --> 00:00:46.136
[Ding]

00:00:46.136 --> 00:00:46.969
- Low beams?

00:00:46.969 --> 00:00:47.802
- [Man] Yeah.

00:00:47.802 --> 00:00:49.339
- Well, when do you use the fog lights?

00:00:49.339 --> 00:00:51.965
When driving in fog,
don't use your fog lights

00:00:51.965 --> 00:00:53.406
whatever you do.

00:00:53.406 --> 00:00:55.584
- Which of the following
is the most effective

00:00:55.584 --> 00:00:56.919
in avoiding a collision?

00:00:56.919 --> 00:00:59.481
The answer is don't drive.

00:00:59.481 --> 00:01:02.524
- A. Keeping your lights on at all times.

00:01:02.524 --> 00:01:04.397
B. Wearing a seat belt.

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:07.556
C. Keeping a cushion
of space at all times.

00:01:07.556 --> 00:01:09.664
- By keeping a cushion of space.

00:01:09.664 --> 00:01:12.231
- Oh C, keeping a cushion
of space at all times.

00:01:12.231 --> 00:01:14.011
- [Man] Correct.

00:01:14.011 --> 00:01:15.528
- What's a cushion of space?

00:01:15.528 --> 00:01:17.089
I sleep on a cushion of space.

00:01:17.089 --> 00:01:21.235
What, my bed is gonna keep me
from colliding with people?

00:01:21.235 --> 00:01:23.087
I don't know, will it?

00:01:23.087 --> 00:01:25.254
- White-painted curb means

00:01:26.334 --> 00:01:27.837
Seriously.

00:01:27.837 --> 00:01:31.227
Means, A. Loading zone
for freight or passengers.

00:01:31.227 --> 00:01:34.200
B. Loading zone for
passengers or mail only.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.602
C. Loading zone for freight only.

00:01:36.602 --> 00:01:39.029
A. Loading zone for
freight and passengers.

00:01:39.029 --> 00:01:39.862
(buzz)

00:01:39.862 --> 00:01:40.901
Goddammit, oops.

00:01:40.901 --> 00:01:42.966
I live in New York!

00:01:42.966 --> 00:01:44.773
We don't drive.

00:01:44.773 --> 00:01:46.666
Okay, first of all that's not true,

00:01:46.666 --> 00:01:49.366
because the post office person in my

00:01:49.366 --> 00:01:51.365
neighborhood never
parks on the white curb.

00:01:51.365 --> 00:01:54.525
They always find my car and block it.

00:01:54.525 --> 00:01:56.053
- How many drinks does it take

00:01:56.053 --> 00:01:57.461
to impair your driving?

00:01:57.461 --> 00:01:58.536
Can I just get this right 'cause

00:01:58.536 --> 00:01:59.578
I don't drink?

00:01:59.578 --> 00:02:01.279
- More than three drinks.

00:02:01.279 --> 00:02:03.648
It depends on the person's
height and weight.

00:02:03.648 --> 00:02:04.481
One Drink.

00:02:04.481 --> 00:02:05.784
I'm sure it's one drink

00:02:05.784 --> 00:02:07.592
can impair your driving.

00:02:07.592 --> 00:02:08.425
- What?

00:02:08.425 --> 00:02:09.897
One drink.

00:02:09.897 --> 00:02:10.730
You're right.

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:12.199
You should never drive if you've

00:02:12.199 --> 00:02:13.492
had a drink.

00:02:13.492 --> 00:02:14.877
- What is a "No Zone"?

00:02:14.877 --> 00:02:16.341
A. A no-parking zone?

00:02:16.341 --> 00:02:19.205
B. A no-stopping-or-unloading zone?

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:20.859
C. None of the above.

00:02:20.859 --> 00:02:22.230
I'm saying none of the above unless

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:24.516
it's me trying to avoid eating cake.

00:02:24.516 --> 00:02:26.123
That's a no zone.

00:02:26.123 --> 00:02:27.640
- Okay, I'm gonna go
with none of the above

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:28.903
because there's a none of the above.

00:02:28.903 --> 00:02:30.048
You always choose the none of the above

00:02:30.048 --> 00:02:31.343
if there is one, right?

00:02:31.343 --> 00:02:33.774
- How many feet must you
stop before a crosswalk?

00:02:33.774 --> 00:02:34.821
Oh man.

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:35.804
- A. Five feet.

00:02:35.804 --> 00:02:36.637
B. Ten feet.

00:02:36.637 --> 00:02:37.785
C. Fifteen feet.

00:02:37.785 --> 00:02:39.099
Oh my God, these people are dead

00:02:39.099 --> 00:02:39.932
in my world.

00:02:39.932 --> 00:02:40.765
I don't know.

00:02:40.765 --> 00:02:41.821
- I mean, as long as you stop by

00:02:41.821 --> 00:02:42.654
the crosswalk.

00:02:42.654 --> 00:02:43.678
Isn't that normally pretty good?

00:02:43.678 --> 00:02:44.856
- I'm gonna say five feet.

00:02:44.856 --> 00:02:45.845
- Five feet.

00:02:45.845 --> 00:02:46.939
- [Man] Correct

00:02:46.939 --> 00:02:47.998
- Five feet?

00:02:47.998 --> 00:02:49.343
Five feet is nothing.

00:02:49.343 --> 00:02:51.930
Do you people want me to hurt some people?

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:53.426
- Before changning lanes on a freeway,

00:02:53.426 --> 00:02:55.336
you should signal for at least:

00:02:55.336 --> 00:02:56.507
- A. Five seconds.

00:02:56.507 --> 00:02:57.585
B. Ten Seconds.

00:02:57.585 --> 00:02:59.285
C. Fifteen Seconds.

00:02:59.285 --> 00:03:00.770
- That I think depends on your age,

00:03:00.770 --> 00:03:02.029
'cause if you're a hundred and ten

00:03:02.029 --> 00:03:03.114
I think you just always drive with

00:03:03.114 --> 00:03:04.292
a signal on, right?

00:03:04.292 --> 00:03:05.474
- Five seconds.

00:03:05.474 --> 00:03:06.307
[Ding]

00:03:06.307 --> 00:03:08.269
- [Man] Yep, right, wow.

00:03:08.269 --> 00:03:10.936
[Celebratory Music And Applauds]

00:03:12.011 --> 00:03:14.867
- Emoji of a nail and emoji of a hammer.

00:03:14.867 --> 00:03:15.700
Nailed it.

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:17.144
- So I just failed?

00:03:17.144 --> 00:03:18.268
- [Man] Yeah.

00:03:18.268 --> 00:03:20.158
- I'm scared to be on the road with me.

00:03:20.158 --> 00:03:22.694
- I will never get my driver's license.

00:03:22.694 --> 00:03:23.966
- I'm gonna go get in my car now

00:03:23.966 --> 00:03:24.846
and drive anyway.

00:03:24.846 --> 00:03:25.751
So I don't really care,

00:03:25.751 --> 00:03:27.334
so forget you guys.

00:03:28.744 --> 00:03:29.916
- The thing with the fog,

00:03:29.916 --> 00:03:32.499
the driving in fog or whatever.

00:03:34.345 --> 00:03:36.729
Alright what do you do
when you drive in fog?

00:03:36.729 --> 00:03:38.392
I dunno, pull over, listen to music

00:03:38.392 --> 00:03:39.225
until it's gone.

00:03:39.225 --> 00:03:40.266
Like, who's driving in fog?

00:03:40.266 --> 00:03:41.365
What am I Batman?

00:03:41.365 --> 00:03:42.350
I don't know.

